# /etc/newsyslog.d/docling.conf -- rotation for the Mac docling-service
# (RFC-052 R1 AC9, task 1.10). Rendered by install-logging.sh (@LOG_DIR@,
# @OWNER@ substituted).
#
# service.log: 10 MB x 5, rotated by rename. The service writes it through
# PAGEINDEX_LOG_FILE -> logging.handlers.WatchedFileHandler, which reopens the
# path once the inode changes, so no signal is needed (N) and none is safe:
# launchd would restart the service mid-conversion. Alloy follows the rename.
# launchd.log / alloy.log hold only launchd-captured stdout/stderr (crash
# output); launchd keeps their fd, so after a rotation those land in .0 until
# the next restart -- acceptable for crash-only files, never for service.log.
#
# logfilename                      [owner:group]  mode count size(KB) when flags
@LOG_DIR@/service.log              @OWNER@        644  5     10240    *    NC
@LOG_DIR@/launchd.log              @OWNER@        644  2     10240    *    NC
@LOG_DIR@/alloy.log                @OWNER@        644  2     10240    *    NC
